WEBVTT

NOTE LUMO, The Gospel of Luke 9:18-62 (Arclight 6_GOLuke2610), en.
NOTE Timings: whisper.cpp small -dtw small per speech burst on the isolated dialogue (dialoguenhance centre channel), first word on the burst start, 2026-10-31.

1
00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:40.550
As they were walking along the road,

2
00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:44.100
a man said to him, I will follow you wherever you go.

3
00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:49.800
Jesus replied, Foxes have dens and birds have nests,

4
00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:53.300
but the Son of Man has no place to lay his head.

5
00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:00.450
He said to another man, Follow me.

6
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:06.750
But he replied, Lord, first let me go and bury my father.

7
00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:11.510
Jesus said to him, Let the dead bury their own dead,

8
00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:16.750
but you go and proclaim the kingdom of God.

9
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:24.450
Still another said, I will follow you, Lord;

10
00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:28.050
but first let me go back and say goodbye to my family.

11
00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:36.360
Jesus replied, No one who puts a hand to the plow

12
00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:39.350
and looks back is fit for service in the kingdom of God.
